Fixed in `tokio-stream/src/stream_map.rs:687`:

```rust
fn size_hint(&self) -> (usize, Option<usize>) {
    let mut ret: (usize, Option<usize>) = (0, Some(0));

    for (_, stream) in &self.entries {
        let hint = stream.size_hint();

        ret.0 = ret.0.saturating_add(hint.0);

        match (ret.1, hint.1) {
            (Some(a), Some(b)) => ret.1 = a.checked_add(b),
            (Some(_), None) => ret.1 = None,
            _ => {}
        }
    }

    ret
}
```

- The lower bound now saturates at `usize::MAX` instead of panicking on `+`.
- The upper bound uses `checked_add`, degrading to `None` (unknown) on overflow, which is the correct `Stream` contract answer — no `usize` value can express the true bound. Once `None`, it stays `None`.
- The explicit type annotation on `ret` is needed so the integer literals aren't ambiguous for the method calls.

`size_hint_overflow` now passes, along with the rest of the tokio-stream suite (no failures).
